  strings           — 9 keys (7 web + stale + openHint).
  AdapterTests / PollingTests / Tests — 38 tests.

States (web's REAL branches reproduced + the P4 freshness leaf — no fabricated chrome):
  • loading/initial → `connecting` (web `unknown`): muted HelpCircle "API" chip ("Connecting…" in tooltip)
  • ready           → `online` (emerald) / `degraded` (amber): "API" + "· {latency}ms"
  • error/offline   → `offline` (rose): "API · Offline" (web buckets a failed/timed-out /healthz to offline);
                      tap → /system-status (diagnose/retry) and the 15s poll auto-retries
  • stale           → a healthy reading aged past the 30s window → dimmed (muted) chip + "· Stale", with the
                      poll cadence + on-appear refreshIfStale() as the auto-refresh (web hook
                      refetchIntervalInBackground:false pauses on background, so the reading genuinely ages)
  • empty           → N/A and NOT fabricated: a health probe always resolves a status; "no value yet" IS the
                      connecting state. Documented (per the 0179/0180 honesty precedent), not faked.

Data binding: useApiHealth + useTranslation bind via the shared P1/S8 state-holder layer
(ConnectionSegmentModel over a ConnectionSegmentSource — PollingConnectionSegmentSource in production, the
host injecting its /healthz probe). NO direct HTTP in the view.

i18n: 9/9 keys declared == used (0 dead, 0 missing). All 7 web-source keys present verbatim
(short/ok/degraded/offline/unknown/tooltip/aria) + 2 native P4-leaf keys (stale, openHint). No English
literals in the Swift sources — every label resolves through the P1/S10 facade.

Accessibility: the segment is one focusable button; its VoiceOver label is the web aria-label
("API connection status: {state} ({latency}ms)"), with the .help tooltip mirroring the web <Tooltip>; an
open hint + .isButton trait are added; the dot + glyph are decorative (web aria-hidden); the stale tone is
muted so colour is never the sole encoder (the "· Stale" marker carries it too). Dynamic Type via the token
fonts; no bespoke animation (reduce-motion safe).

Telemetry: emits `view.opened` with surface slug "ConnectionSegment" exactly once per model instance
(P1/S11), idempotent across appear/disappear churn.

